ce: Internal audit simulation and log quality testing is a standard compliance practice that does not violate legal norms or business sensibilities.\n\nEffectiveness evidence: The sandbox validates that existing logs would support post-market monitoring and root-cause reconstruction, which contributes to meeting Article 12 but does not itself install the required logging capabilities.\n\nApplicability evidence: Ensuring logs are sufficient for traceability directly addresses the mandate to enable post-market monitoring and regulatory audit readiness under Article 12.\n\nOriginality evidence: Combining synthetic failure injection with engineer challenges and a log traceability score is unusual and shows imagination beyond routine log checks.\n\nParadigm_relatedness evidence: The proposal adds new tools and processes for compliance testing while still treating logging as a separate compliance practice rather than redefining R&D.\n\nProvide scores.\n\nLet's output.",
