ce structured output.\n\nMaybe:\n\nid: P2315\napplicability_evidence: ...\napplicability: 4\n...\n\nProvide six.\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's craft sentences.\n\napplicability_evidence: The suite directly tests whether logging meets Article 12 and Annex III requirements, which is the core of meeting the mandate.\napplicability: 4\n\neffectiveness_evidence: Verifying logs catches failures before deployment but does not itself create the mandated logging capabilities.\neffectiveness: 3\n\noriginality_evidence: Compliance unit testing for AI logs is unusual in R&D labs and shows imaginative application of software testing to regulation.\noriginality: 3\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: It adds a testing tool and process around logging without changing how R&D relates to compliance obligations.\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\n\nacceptability_evidence: Building internal validation tests is a common, legally neutral engineering practice that violates no norms.\nacceptability: 4\n\nimplementability_evidence: Creating synthetic stress tests and automated log checks requires moderate engineering work but is reasonably feasible for an R&D lab.\nimplementability: 3\n\nCheck anchors.\n\nPossibly originality could be 2 = interesting. Might be common? Hmm. Let's keep 3.\n\nParadigm relatedness 2 correct.\n\nOk output.\n\n",
