ners...)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance\n\nProposal introduces automated pipeline integrating MLflow with template generator. This is new tools but still treats compliance as logging practice. Slightly paradigm stretching? It integrates R&D logs directly to EU requirements, maybe changes relationship. Could be 2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice. Hmm.\n\nOriginality (1-4):\n4 = not expressed before AND ingenious\n3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imagination\n2 = interesting\n1 = common, mundane\n\nAutomated documentation pipeline is somewhat common idea. Might be interesting but not rare? Many labs use MLflow. Probably originality 2 = interesting. Or 3 = unusual interesting shows some imagination. I'd say 2 or 3. Probably 2 = interesting.\n\nLet's decide:\n\nacceptability_evidence: The pipeline automates documentation extraction without violating legal norms or researcher sensibilities.\nacceptability:4\n\nimplementability_evidence: Integrating existing experiment trackers with a template generator requires moderate engineering effort but uses off-the-shelf tools.\nimplementability:3\n\napplicability_evidence: The proposal directly targets the record-keeping and technical documentation burdens implied by Recital 71 for high-risk AI systems.\napplicability:4? Let's think. Stated problem is logging mandate. This is about documentation pipeline mapping R&D logs to requirements. That is directly related to meeting logging mandate via records. Might be 4.\n\nEffectiveness_evidence: Automating documentation reduces manual paperwork and supports compliance but does not by itself guarantee the automatic event logging required by Article 12(1).\neffectiveness:3\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: It introduces new tooling for documentation yet keeps complia