l, interesting; shows some imagination\n2 = interesting\n1 = common mundane boring\n\nDeveloping metrics to quantify how effectively logs reconstruct decision path, forensic analyses of failures... publish. That's unusual? Might be interesting but not extremely ingenious. Could be 3? Or 2? Probably unusual, interesting; shows some imagination -> 3.\n\nEffectiveness (1-4):\n4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability\n3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution of problem (helps but partial)\n2 = unreasonable or unlikely to solve problem\n1 = solves unrelated problem\n\nProblem: lab must decide how to respond: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Approval means committing scarce implementation resources.\n\nProposal is research project to develop metrics, publish findings. Will that solve logging mandate? It contributes to understanding logs but does not implement logging capability required by Article 12. So it will contribute? Might be partial solution to compliance? It addresses traceability but not mandatory automatic recording. Effectiveness: reasonable and will contribute to solution? Might be only partial, doesn't ensure logs are recorded per Article 12 1-3. Could be 3? Or 2 = unreasonable or unlikely to solve problem. The stated problem is meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Adapting R&D to study traceability could be adaptation. But does it meet logging mandate? No. Effectiveness maybe 3: contributes to solution (better logs) but not full compliance.\n\nApplicability (1-4):\n4 = solves identified problem directly related\n3 = solves implied problem related\n2 = may have some benefit within special situation...\n1 = ...\n\nIdea applies to traceability which is part of logging mandate. It solves implied problem of meaningful traceability. Could be 3? Or 4? Identified problem is meet logging mandate. The proposal does not directly meet mandate (recording events). It addresses post-market monitoring etc. Might be 3: solves implied problem related.\n\nImplementability (1-4):\n4 = easy low cost\n3 = some changes, reasonably feasible\n2 = significant change expensive/difficult but not impossible\n1 = totally infeasible\n\nFormal research project, forensic analyses, publish peer-reviewed. Requires resources, team time. Some changes, reasonably feasible? Might be significant change. Could be 2 or 3. Probably 3 = some changes, reasonably feasible measures. Research project is feasible for R&D lab. Maybe 3.\n\nAcceptability (1-4):\n4 = common strategies violate no norms\n3 = somewhat uncommon unusual strategies do not offend sensibilities\n2 = offends somewhat\n1 = radically violates\n\nPublishing research on transparency is acceptable. Common? Might be 4 = common strategies that violate no norms or sensibilities. Or 3 = somewhat uncommon. Research project is acceptable. I'd say 4.\n\nNeed one sentence evidence each then score.\n\nProvide JSON? Probably output with id and fields.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nP2371\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 3\n\netc.\n\nMake sure order listed: paradigm_relatedness, originality, effectiveness, applicability, implementability, acceptability\n\nProvide evidence sentence then score.\n\nReturn rating echoing its id exactly.\n\nProbably format:\nid: P2371\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 3\n...\n\nLet's do that.\n\n",
